    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54-a1">

                <pb facs="0189" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg55"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 112.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Cotegipe to
                        Mr. Jarvis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">24th of October</hi>,
                            1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In addition to my note of the 16th of September last, I have the honor to inform
                    Mr. T. J. Jarvis, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United
                    States of America, that the department of agriculture, commerce, and public
                    works has just stated to me that, by decree No. 9872 of the 17th of last month,
                    there was extended for six months more the term prescribed to the Pedro the
                    Second American Telegraph and Cable Company for the submersion of the submarine
                    cable, and that there can be granted only six additional months for the
                    completion of the works, if the company shows that it has not been able to
                    complete them within the term now granted on account of main force.</p>
                <p>I take the opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. de
                            Cotegipe.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
